\": \"U7 MS1/AD0 and MS2/AD1 are tied to +3V3, while the same pins on U5 and U6 are left unconnected. The three TMC2209s are configured inconsistently.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The three identical TMC2209 drivers should have matching address/microstep strapping, and their inputs should not float.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U7\\\") (pin \\\"10\\\") (pinfunction \\\"MS2/AD1\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"146\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(U6-MS1{slash}AD0-Pad9)\\\")\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"U5 and U6 have floating UART address inputs, which may give unreliable driver addressing or microstep behaviour. U7 uses a different address than the other two.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows the Nutrient-B TMC2209 (U7) A+ output pin 24 and the H9 connector's A+ terminal both tied to GND, with no /A_NB+ net, while the other two drivers route OA1 to their connectors. This is a clear short that disables the Nutrient-B pump coil.\"\n}",
